msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:33
#: 6c39712b2aba48c09439d18c820d0d78
msgid "The Flip frame kit is $89.00 from Hoverthings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:34
#: 291974af468442199e1ecfbaf8e3e1c7
msgid "In addition to the standard Sport frame kit I also purchased an extended tab pair of center frame pieces and some extra 7/8\" stand offs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:37
#: 94197b908923424c9f31d6b65e64ad25
msgid "It is billed as being nearly indestructible and short of direct Nuclear blast effects, they are probably right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:39
#: 286c07fda9aa43dea6aec648b73c0e79
msgid "The frame arms on these Flips are billed as being incredibly stiff and incredibly strong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:41
#: 752fcd26687e4509b028fb04139edbf4
msgid "The arms are CNC milled high density 1/4\" thick fiberglass and are very stiff, they should be able to withstand a lot of punishment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:43
#: 73a030745a1c4b88a348f986f42d5332
msgid "The frame centers are also very strong and stiff fiberglass and it it seems likely all of it is G10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:45
#: 0bd01ad868e54753a189c4579a150be9
msgid "This is a small 380 size frame and will accommodate 10\" propellers (Right between the Flamewheel F330 and F450.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:52
#: 862ef06411dc49ee87adf46608137714
msgid "What to get"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:54
#: 21a97c90715a452aaa9e15411628d5ce
msgid "A `Hoverthings Flip Sport Frame <https://www.amazon.com/HoverThings-Flip-Frame-Black-Orange/dp/B00HZTN6GO/>`__ (approx $89.00 USD)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:59
#: 94c0c62a8ccb4a8eb8fb393a08e675c1
msgid "`Two tabbed center sections <http://www.hoverthings.com/flip4tabblack>`__ and *eight 7/8\" standoffs* (e.g. `similar to these <http://hoverthings.com/standoff-nylon-f-f/>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:60
#: dadc763000bd4a049e0aa632805fb4fb
msgid "Four DJI motors for Flamewheel from `Amain Hobby <https://www.amainhobbies.com/dji-multirotor-replacement-brushless-motor-dji-motor01/p235238>`__ for $24.00 each."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:62
#: fd4a1fa903734281b0217de3c6aee8fa
msgid "A 20 or 25 Amp four in one ESC from `Off the Grid Water <http://mymobilemms.com/OFFTHEGRIDWATER.CA/ESC/4-in-1-Speed-Control-Quad-HOBBYWING-Quattro-Skywalker-25A-X-41?cPath=2_4>`__ for $40.00."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:64
#: 02efed32fafa4ef7a738c018d563f23a
msgid "A :ref:`Pixhawk <common-pixhawk-overview>` compatible autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:65
#: 9db24a4030714bf6a3983ea310499727
msgid "A :ref:`GPS and Compass Module <common-positioning-landing-page>` module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:66
#: 0f68154a063c4a27929d26e19ec9cd61
msgid "Two `normal <https://www.rcdude.com/product-p/gf-1045-c.htm>`__ and two `reverse <https://www.rcdude.com/product-p/gf-1045r-blk.htm>`__ rotation DJI compatible Gemfan 10\" carbon filled propellers from RC Dude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:70
#: b8c89ff9aba346a3816c432bd28a4825
msgid "A 2600 to `4000mah LiPo battery <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-battery-nano-tech-4000mah-3s-25-50c-lipo-pack-xt-60.html?___store=en_us>`__ that fits between the 2 bottom plates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:72
#: 5e0d9b8ef41c4d14a58c795927c6c920
msgid "PPM-Sum compatible receiver that works with your RC transmitter: `FRSky <http://www.valuehobby.com/radio-systems-servos/receivers/frsky-receiver-telemetry.html>`__\\ `(Delta 8) <http://www.valuehobby.com/frysky-delta-8.html>`__, Futaba SBus or Spektrum satellite recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:76
#: 16486d98d78448558be9993a00db6175
msgid "For a PX4 system: A `Pad of Kyousho Zeal Antivibration gel <https://www.amainhobbies.com/kyosho-zeal-vibration-absorption-gyro-reciever-mounting-gel-1-sheet-kyoz8006/p19713>`__ and four nylon or aluminum 1 1/2\" threaded standoffs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:83
#: d3a7eb98c394409abc62345985cb3c78
msgid "Assembling the frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:85
#: 47bd970f737e4f6fb82a55d590642e76
msgid "There are two different construction methods depending on whether you are using a Pixhawk or a PX4FMU/PX4IO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:87
#: ce348d504c9748db8eca98d078fc1577
msgid "For the Pixhawk you will use the second untabbed center plate on top as shown above, for a PX4FMU/PX4IO you will not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:89
#: 40b246216cef4ce58ac9beb31a90b123
msgid "Construction procedure is as follows (Use blue Locktite on all machine screws.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:91
#: 86902508146348b8a049e05df7f56243
msgid "Assemble the 2 tabbed center sections with four 7/8\" standoffs on the 2 holes an inch apart 2\" in from the end on 2 opposing sides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:93
#: bfaaa842116f4caabfd73940f8761955
msgid "Mount the arms to the top of one of the tabbed center frames using the short standoffs above the arm and use locktite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:96
#: 2c9d8e31a7a446ee9d1c9dbc97f7f4bf
msgid "Ensure that the standoffs mounting the two tabbed frame sections are on either side of your copter, not front to back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:98
#: 60f285a61f114dffa74fbfb35370139f
msgid "Put the longer screws up through the tabbed plate and arms (2 on the outside 1 in the middle towards the middle) into the short standoffs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:102
#: 907771405a8446d2be01f3d5ddf2d513
msgid "Insert and your four in one ESC in between the arms with the excess Motor wire wrapped around the ESC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:105
#: 64ddcf8bcae4429cb732fb21f8308f0f
msgid "Leave about 3 inches of the 3 ESC motor wires sticking out under each arm (I also braided each motors wires on mine.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:107
#: 746f3b84abf84f89843173ff8bd7450a
msgid "Leave the ESC signal wires and power leads sticking out the back (between the 2 black arms on mine.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:110
#: 8037fe8e006f40e69b48ed233c7f6834
msgid "Put an untabbed frame plate on top of your frame and secure with 12 screws to the top of the standoffs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:112
#: feeeb9742a2a4ce48fe75705f30e66ce
msgid "Install your DJI motors onto the frame arms with the supplied screws (use Locktite) with the motor wires facing the copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:114
#: 26d9fdf63cbb4494b099f9ff5dde0e7d
msgid "Thread the motor wires through the top frame arm opening and connect to the ESC wires (tuck excess lead into frame)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:121
#: ff049ca04b884758aff9010f4aa5dc10
msgid "Installing the Pixhawk autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:123
#: e445908d85be41d393a4ad89663ed3db
msgid "If you are using a Pixhawk, mount the 4 remaining 7/8\" long standoffs, directly over the ones securing the bottom frame plates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:125
#: f95f8e3fcb7a4c05997cfd4c1612b19f
msgid "Place a 1\" square of the Double-sided foam tape that came with the Pixhawk on the bottom of it at each corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:127
#: d3d9168a43f14ee3826f86ab1ff5b6e4
msgid "Adhere the Pixhawk to the top of the frame with the arrow pointing to the front (between the 2 orange arms on mine)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:129
#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:179
#: 5412f8529f1745c7b3d3cfa9ad98e992
#: cdd0e9339aea4ab5b97c2784e0118138
msgid "Drill a hole through the top 2 frame plates near a frame arm near the edge on one side to accommodate the \"safety\" button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:131
#: 8a7a9d02fc3046bab1c997b812aeb848
msgid "Also mount the buzzer on the top frame member on one side where it will not interfere with a receiver installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:133
#: 227c107825f847c49b54717a1dac43c7
msgid "Connect the 3DR power module to the Pixhawk connector and attach the power module out of the way also."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:135
#: 512747a97b3a481eab7358cc10d46b14
msgid "Solder the other end of the power module wires into a battery connector along with the ESC battery leads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:137
#: 6335451b2697438787e61ae1847e1540
msgid "Install the ESC's signal leads into the Pixhawk (Main Out) servo connectors (signal wire on top)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:140
#: e306f889d13048ae84c4bfeb3ee605f1
msgid "Red wire into 1, Orange into 2, White into 3 (with red and black below) and Brown into 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:143
#: 93af629c87764dc79d519ec4208d8d1a
msgid "Install the GPS and compass wires into the GPS/Compass module and the Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:145
#: 7eee920b728449008e218e74b21d314d
msgid "Mount your receiver with double sided tape or Velcro on the top frame member to one side of (and not touching) the Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:148
#: 1109ab817a1848f490f1ea6c8f8a2609
msgid "Run a single servo lead from the PPM-Sum output of the receiver to the left side (RC) input of the Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:150
#: 1eef08c13ee148c4b71e678fb88abbfe
msgid "Or if it is a Spektrum Satellite run the Spektrum receiver lead to the Spektrum socket on top of the Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:153
#: 2fc0d039a1314da39d2f306a7c66ce21
msgid "Mount the top untabbed frame member over the Pixhawk to the 7/8\" standoffs you already installed above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:155
#: 4ac347f964a64895ad68e84eaa27650a
msgid "Mount the GPS module to the top center of the top frame plate using double sided tape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:159
#: dcd411f7e0cb4d99b1388b78ed5fe149
msgid "Installing the PX4FMU/PX4IO autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:161
#: fb3d32f5c2974338b4bba7082cab6a85
msgid "If you are using a PX4 we can't use the top frame plate but can construct a little hard top if desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:163
#: 058c47c826a44f6a8e300838e14453b8
msgid "Cut a 2\" by 2\" rectangle from scrap plastic or fiberglass to support the PX4FMU/PX4IO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:165
#: 97cde56af5c94b94906ce10632b5829b
msgid "Drill 4 holes in the rectangle that line up with the mounting hole in the PX4 board (roughly centered)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:167
#: 4f7c2f0ea8d54559aae5aee3e527f0be
msgid "using 4 of the supplied black screws, mount 4 standoffs to the rectangle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:169
#: 3b2b7299189f4f16834a7b5e9a8ecba7
msgid "Insert the PX4FMU board (connector side up) over the 4 standoff studs and (carefully) screw 4 more standoffs over them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:171
#: 30bfd9210573472e947cb4b3640cf1fe
msgid "Carefully fasten 4 nuts over the exposed studs securing the PX4FMU/PX4IO modules to the rectangle you made."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:173
#: 0c5cc5c973d24b5d9bfe784595f1a957
msgid "Place the PX4IO board over the PX4FMU board so that the connector is aligned and push down over the studs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:175
#: f4302395b4314ac8ba3793fc09d7685a
msgid "Place a 3/4\" square piece of the Kyosho zeal at each edge of the \"rectangle\" between the standoff screws."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:177
#: 207d454c40b54476bc867b7ac6c8c83e
msgid "Adhere the rectangle to the center of the top of the frame with the servo connector facing to the rear (between the black frame arms)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:181
#: 87c529a1c7cb4628ad8c51e1c64d42a9
msgid "Also mount the buzzer on the top frame member behind the PX4FMU/PX4IO stack such that it does not touch the \"rectangle\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:183
#: 52c6921eb66443a18db51938073aee57
msgid "Insert the power connector into the PX4IO board and solder the power leads and the ESC power leads to a battery connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:185
#: 5edb096c880d447289bcdc2c9f5d8d6f
msgid "Connect the buzzer and \"Safety\" button leads to the PX4FMU/PX4IO boards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:186
#: 1b2d90ba08614cb59a82e46c8e64c98f
msgid "Install the ESC's signal leads into the PX4IO board servo connectors (signal wire on top)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:190
#: 50361e3c3b9f4c358dc730c83db9346a
msgid "Red wire = right pins, Orange = 2nd from right, White = 3rd from right (with red and black below) and Brown = 4 from right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:193
#: b5495e5aef2b4d1eb88e201819ab768f
msgid "Mount your receiver with double sided tape or Velcro on the top frame member to one side of (and not touching) the \"rectangle\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:196
#: bfec8b3fc9fc4c13aaf140f7a47b226f
msgid "Ensure that your receiver does not block the USB connector on the side of the PX4FMU board (put it on the other side)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:198
#: c53500adc6bc40858364ec8b7545434e
msgid "Run a single servo lead from the PPM-Sum output of the receiver to the far left side of the PX4IO servo connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:200
#: ba22a874b12e477d91e5f90ab070ef2c
msgid "Or if it is a Spektrum Satellite receiver run the Spektrum receiver lead to the Spektrum socket on top of the Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:203
#: 80a5fca6d8d14652b343416811db56e9
msgid "To use the remaining frame plate as a top cover screw the 4 standoffs to the top of the frame using existing holes near the edge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:206
#: 4f5d95dfdbd94fdfb54166aea5857674
msgid "Screw the plate to the 4 standoffs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:208
#: 08be0f1bc72946878791eea7a482bd6f
msgid "You can make your own top cover from a rectangle of plastic or fiberglass (I used Plexiglass, transparent is useful)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:211
#: 9333716410554747afa770c462df8892
msgid "Ensure that the rectangle is of appropriate size and shape to permit you to secure the standoffs to the top plate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:213
#: c7ddb15e427143cfa10140032622959c
msgid "Drill holes in the rectangle at the appropriate locations and if needed into the top frame member as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:215
#: fcb49f6069c7484d8ad315a266289488
msgid "Attach the standoffs to the top frame member and to the Rectangular top you have made."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:218
#: 666c60f63e7d4c03882bc020cc0c7018
msgid "Adhere the GPS/Compass module to the center of the top of the top cover (it doesn't matter which way it is facing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:221
#: 2aa3dc20835c4a518d86b62561731ad9
msgid "Connect the GPS / Compass module to the PX4IO with the supplied wiring cables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:223
#: fc7153527054460b90e2c45a4a1d7ba0
msgid "Note my setup uses an older style UBlox standalone GPS which I have mounted directly to the PX4 stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:234
#: e8c7ef5b38e44e9e88a6ded2b5993a41
msgid "Final assembly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:236
#: f7ad18dfc7114eada6384a9be815a12d
msgid "Mount the battery between the lower frame sections and secure it with a Velcro strap inserted through the bottom frame plate slots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:238
#: e09784982d484bad8b4a2fd65904762b
msgid "Route and secure the wires and cables with Zip Ties as shown to prevent snagging on the propellers or anything else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:240
#: 642c310db7bc4b2b98659b4cb3c35046
msgid "Ensure that the battery cable is secure but accessible to be plugged in when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:248
#: a52bc948b54142f9812bc28617f5ff64
msgid "Setup and additions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:250
#: 4e6265c532964793b98d19f364eb3b4c
msgid "Your Flip can now be configured as described elsewhere in this wiki for Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:252
#: bebdaa14b62a4a979868cf42e2d4f990
msgid "There is space for a 3DR telemetry radio and / or an OSD and FPV transmitter between the 2 side tabs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:255
#: 40db8ca696894cb0a4c14380be36b423
msgid "An FPV camera may easily be mounted in front of the battery between the 2 front tabs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:257
#: d00bbbc8c48942b2b05b5cdd64bb8b75
msgid "If you use FPV keep its transmitter and antenna well away from the GPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:260
#: 745bbc53abf845ed89fa36d8da4906ce
msgid "The Flip has more than adequate power to support a GoPro camera with a brushless gimbal and the necessary extended landing gear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/hoverthings-flip-sport-quadcopter.rst:262
#: 0fe85e3b004f48119532a952451e2be7
msgid "I have had several crashes and only managed to break 2 props while trying (unsuccessfully) to cut down a 80' bull pine tree with them."
msgstr ""

